---
import PageShell from '../../components/nav/PageShell.astro';
import { groups } from '../../data/checks';
import { CRATE_URL } from '../../consts';

const title = 'Checks | DeepCausality Quantum';
const description =
  'Every check in deep_causality_quantum: the question it decides, the error a rejection raises, when it passes without examining anything, and whether Lean proves it or tests witness it.';

const mark = { proved: 'proved in Lean', partial: 'proved in part', tested: 'tested', decision: 'by decision' } as const;
const cls = { proved: 'validated', partial: 'partial', tested: 'measured', decision: 'nongoal' } as const;
---
<PageShell title={title} description={description} path="/checks/">
  <header class="doc-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Checks</p>
    <h1>What each check decides, and what a failure names.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Each entry names a check, the subjects that run it and the question it decides. It then
      gives what a rejection carries, when the check passes without examining anything (a
      Vacuous verdict), and what backs it. None of the fourteen entries is fully proved in
      Lean: two are proved in part, eleven are tested, and one is a decision the crate records.
    </p>
  </header>

  {groups.map((g) => (
    <section class="doc-sec" id={g.id}>
      <h2>{g.title}</h2>
      <p class="glede">{g.lede}</p>
      <dl class="checks">
        {g.checks.map((c) => (
          <div class="check">
            <dt>
              <code class="cname">{c.name}</code>
              <span class="on">{c.on}</span>
              <span class={`status status-${cls[c.backing]}`}>{mark[c.backing]}</span>
            </dt>
            <dd>
              <p class="q">{c.question}</p>
              <dl class="meta">
                <div><dt>On rejection</dt><dd>{c.rejection}</dd></div>
                <div><dt>When vacuous</dt><dd>{c.vacuous}</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Evidence</dt><dd>{c.evidence}</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Source</dt><dd><a href={`${CRATE_URL}/${c.source}`}><code>{c.source}</code></a></dd></div>
              </dl>
            </dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </section>
  ))}

  <section class="doc-sec" id="verdicts">
    <h2>How does a measurement become a verdict?</h2>
    <p>
      The crate reads a verdict from a state and a measurement projection <code>P</code>. The
      Born rule <code>Tr(Pρ)</code> gives a probability verdict, and the projection itself is a
      proposition in the lattice of projections. The operators carry no verdict of their own,
      because general effects (<code>0 ≤ E ≤ I</code>) form only an effect algebra, which has
      partial meet and join.
    </p>
    <p>
      The lattice of projections is bounded, has the orthocomplement <code>I − P</code> and
      satisfies the orthomodular law. It fails distributivity, as probability verdicts fail
      excluded middle. The Rust carrier and its law tests are complete; the Lean statement that
      the lattice is orthomodular is a deferred target.
    </p>
    <p class="next-links">
      <a href="/proof/#deferred">The deferred targets →</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</PageShell>

<style>
  .glede { color: var(--fg-1); max-width: var(--measure); margin: 0 0 var(--space-5); }

  .checks { margin: 0; }
  .check { padding: var(--space-5) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line-1); }
  .check:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-1); }
  .check > dt { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-4); margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); }
  .cname { background: none; padding: 0; color: var(--fg-0); font-size: var(--t-body); font-weight: var(--fw-heading); }
  .on { color: var(--fg-2); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-eyebrow); letter-spacing: var(--ls-eyebrow); text-transform: uppercase; }
  .check > dd { margin: 0; }
  .q { color: var(--fg-0); margin: 0 0 var(--space-4); max-width: var(--measure); }

  .meta { margin: 0; display: grid; gap: var(--space-2); }
  .meta > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 2px; }
  .meta dt { color: var(--fg-2); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-eyebrow); letter-spacing: var(--ls-eyebrow); text-transform: uppercase; }
  .meta dd { margin: 0; color: var(--fg-1); font-size: var(--t-body-sm); max-width: var(--measure); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .meta > div { grid-template-columns: 11rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--space-4); }
  }
</style>
